<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="50665" href="schedule/2015/spring/CMN/496/50665.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2015" href="schedule/2015.xml">2015</calendarYear><term id="120151" href="schedule/2015/spring.xml">Spring 2015</term><subject id="CMN" href="schedule/2015/spring/CMN.xml">Communication</subject><course id="496" href="schedule/2015/spring/CMN/496.xml">Adv Topics in Communication</course></parents><sectionNumber>CJU</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Language &amp; Cognition</sectionTitle><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Explores: (1) how the nature of human communication is shaped by the human ability to learn and use language, and (2) how the nature of human communication is shaped by the properties of the linguistic instruments humans have constructed. Topics include: animal communication; concepts and logic; grammar; language development; human biology and evolution; writing; computing machinery; plans, strategies, and inference  as related to language.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Undergrad - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>CrossListOpen (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2015-01-20Z</startDate><endDate>2015-05-06Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>03:30 PM</start><end>04:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>4053</roomNumber><buildingName>Lincoln Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Jacobs" firstName="C">Jacobs, C</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>